  "description": "Reduces container attack surface by building application images on Google distroless base images that ship only the application runtime - no shell, package manager, or OS utilities - using multi-stage build patterns plus debugging and scanning techniques adapted to distroless. Use when hardening container images, cutting attack surface in a container architecture, or answering an assessment finding about bloated base images. Keywords: distroless, multi-stage build, no shell, nonroot tag, debug image, scratch, attack surface. Do not use for scanning an image for known CVEs - use scanning-docker-images-with-trivy.",
